  "about": "I hope this message finds you well.\nI am Chandrakiran Patel, and I hold a Bachelor's degree in Information Technology and Engineering from CCS (Chaudhary Charan Singh) University, along with a Diploma in Information Technology from Government Girls Polytechnic. I have developed a strong foundation in both theoretical and practical aspects of software development.\n\nCurrently, at JDAAS, I work as a Full Stack .NET Developer, building scalable and responsive web applications using Angular and ASP.NET Core. My responsibilities include developing user interfaces with Angular, TypeScript, HTML, CSS, and Bootstrap, while implementing backend logic, REST APIs, and database integration using ASP.NET Core and MSSQL. I am actively involved in real-world projects and API-driven development.\n\nI am proficient in Angular, ASP.NET Core, MSSQL, TypeScript, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and REST APIs. Additionally, I have experience working with tools such as Visual Studio Code, Git, GitHub, SQL Server Management Studio, Postman, Notepad++, and TortoiseSVN, which support efficient development, version control, and API testing.\n\nIn addition to my experience in web development, I am proficient in HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and ReactJS. I am also skilled with tools such as Visual Studio Code, Git, SQL Server Management Studio. which support efficient development, project management, and API testing. My ability to adapt to new technologies and my passion for innovation make me confident in my ability to contribute effectively to your team.\n\nEarlier in my career, I worked at Magic EdTech, where I contributed to eBook accessibility projects involving MathML, Read-Aloud audio features, and frontend development using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.\n\nI am excited about the opportunity to bring my background in software development and my passion for collaborative, innovative projects to your team.",
